# shir_nodes/deref.node — Deref: read through a reference (`*p`).
#
# GENERIC (Go *p auto-deref reads, Zig p.*, C-like *p). Matching read
# side of AddressOf (see address_of.node for the pair contract):
#   - reference-capable backends render a true dereference
#     (Perl: ${...} / @{...});
#   - value-only backends pass the operand through (snapshot semantics;
#     nil-deref detection stays with guards the frontend already emits,
#     e.g. `p == nil`).
# WRITES through a dereference have no node here by design: they are a
# storage effect, refused by frontends rather than guessed.

node Deref
tag "Deref"
kind expr
field pointer: expr
